<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Appendix: Alternative Encodings in Cosmology and Computation</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">A.1 Effective Fluids and RSVP Field Dynamics</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">The Giani‚Äìvon Marttens‚ÄìCamilleri (2025) model provides a phenomenological recipe for encoding collapsing regions () and voids () as effective fluids with nonzero equations of state. From the RSVP perspective, these terms emerge naturally from field dynamics:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Collapsing modes: regions where the divergence of the vector field is negative (), producing negentropic compression.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Expansive modes: regions where the divergence is positive (), corresponding to entropic expansion.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Coupling terms () represent lamphron‚Äìlamphrodyne transfers of energy between dust, compression, and void expansion.</p>
