<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">5.6 Complexity, Causality, and Finality</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Complexity thresholds (see Section 4) require higher-order causality:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Material ‚Üí Biological: efficient causes insufficient; teleonomic constraints necessary.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Biological ‚Üí Mental: recursive downward causation required; informational teleonomy.</p>
