<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">where  is the kinematical backreaction and  is the averaged spatial curvature.</p>
<hr class="border-border-l2">
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">16.2 Giani‚Äìvon Marttens Effective Fluids</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Instead of directly averaging Einstein‚Äôs equations, Giani et al. model non-linear inhomogeneities (clusters and voids) as effective fluids with their own equations of state:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\dot{\rho}_c + 3H \rho_c (1 + w_c) = C(t),</p>
