<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">w_{\text{tot}} = \frac{\rho_c w_c + \rho_v w_v}{\rho_d + \rho_c + \rho_v}.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">This structure reproduces Buchert‚Äôs  and  terms in an effective-fluid form.</p>
<hr class="border-border-l2">
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">16.3 RSVP Integration: Entropy‚ÄìVector‚ÄìScalar Fields</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">RSVP interprets these backreaction fluids not as phenomenological stand-ins, but as manifestations of scalar (Œ¶), vector (ùíó), and entropy (S) fields. For example:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Collapsing regions (clusters) ‚Üí local minima in Œ¶, high vorticity in ùíó.</p>
