\begin{abstract}
This monograph transforms the original essay into a comprehensive exploration of encoding ratchets‚Äîrepresentational choices that, once standardized, dominate through scalability‚Äîacross cinema, computation, and cosmology. Integrating historical debates on AI scaling, fallibilist naturalism, and recent advances in effective-fluid cosmology \citep{Giani2025}, it argues that scaling amplifies contingent encodings, often marginalizing richer alternatives. Grounded in philosophical frameworks of emergence, downward causation, and orders of nature, the work employs mathematical derivations, historical vignettes, and worked examples to propose the Relativistic Scalar Vector Plenum (RSVP) as a counter-ratchet framework. Extensive appendices provide mathematical formalisms, philosophical notes, and alternative computational architectures, advocating for pluralistic scientific paradigms.
\end{abstract}
