\subsection{Local Metaphysics and Objective Relativism}
Cahoone adapts the Columbia school‚Äôs doctrine of objective relativism, which denies the existence of ‚Äúsimples‚Äù and rejects the ambition to describe ‚Äúthe whole.‚Äù All knowledge is local, fallible, and contextual. A natural complex is always defined by its relations. Thus, metaphysics must be ‚Äúlocal metaphysics‚Äù: a mapping of how domains interrelate, without claiming absolute foundations.
Mathematically, RSVP reflects this principle through sheaf-theoretic encodings: each domain (cosmological, biological, cognitive) corresponds to a local section of the plenum fields, and consistency is enforced only on overlaps. There is no global section (no ‚Äúwhole‚Äù metaphysics), but a patchwork of compatible locals.
